How about when you attempt to fire an arrow and you already have a bow 
in your inventory, you automatically wield it? This mirrors (sort of) 
polearm and pickaxe usage, and also solves the problem that firing 
arrows isn't really intuitive - there is a command to "fire" them, which 
actually just throws them unless you happened to be wielding a bow at 
the same time.

I see two complications with this approach:
1) Which bow to select when you have multiple bows?
2) What if you have an unid'd cursed bow as your only bow?

The solution I propose to these is for the autobow feature to only work 
when exactly one appropriate buc'd launcher and never to autowield an 
unbuc'd launcher.

It's a bit ugly, but so is providing another equipment slot. I'm not 
sure which idea I prefer. :/

